{title: I Thank You With All My Heart}
{subtitle: Psalms 138:1–3}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]I thank you [F7sus4]with all my heart
Before the [Bb]gods I sing your praise
I bow down [Eb]toward your [F7sus4]holy temple
Giving thanks to [Bb]your holy name
Your [Eb]steadfast love [F7sus4]and faithfulness
Exalted [Bb]word above all else
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
On the [Eb]day I called [F7sus4]you answered me
You made me bold with [Bb]strength in my soul
On the [Bb/D]day I [Eb]called you an[F7sus4]swered me
You made me bold with strength in [Bb]my soul
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
All the kings of the earth will [Eb]thank you
[F7sus4]For they have heard the words of your [Bb]mouth
They will sing of the [Bb/D]ways [Eb]of the Lord
[F7sus4]For the glory of the Lord is [Bb]great
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
On the day I [Bb/D]called you [Eb]answered me
[F7sus4]You made me bold with strength in my [Bb]soul
On the day I [Bb/D]called you [Eb]answered me
[F7sus4]You made me bold with strength in my [Bb]soul
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]The Lord is exalted yet [F]he sees the lowly
[Bb]The proud he knows from [Bb/D]afar
You [Eb]have exalted your [F]word above all your [Gm]name
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I thank you with [Eb]all my heart
[F]Before the gods I sing your [Bb]praise
{end_of_verse}
